  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Digital Systems</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">TradeMark Africa&apos;s Digital Trade Systems Portfolio works to eliminate the paper-based, manual processes that continue to make trading more costly and time-consuming than in advanced economies, by investing in digital trade infrastructure that reduces bureaucracy, lowers transaction costs, and improves the predictability and transparency of cross-border commerce. Since 2010, the Portfolio has facilitated over 100 digital trade portals across the continent, including integrated customs management systems, electronic cargo tracking systems, national single windows, and value chain-specific trading platforms for sectors such as tea and coffee, contributing to a reduction in document processing costs. The Portfolio&apos;s current agenda spans five interconnected areas: digitising customs and border management processes in partnership with governments and revenue authorities; deploying ICT solutions that improve market information access and financial inclusion; developing and enhancing e-commerce platforms and digital payment systems to connect buyers and sellers across borders; enhancing the interoperability of customs and trade systems between countries to support integrated corridor management; and harnessing emerging technologies &#x2014; including Artificial Intelligence and distributed ledger systems,  to provide secure, transparent platforms for recording and tracking trade transactions, with a deliberate focus on expanding digital access for women, youth, and small-scale traders..</narrative>
  </description>
